["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/ResponsibilityType/ownership", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Ownership refers to the legal right to control, manage, and benefit from an asset, resource, or responsibility. It establishes authority, accountability, and entitlements over something, whether it's property, a business, intellectual property, or responsibilities.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/follows", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "The `to` Element succeeds the `from` Element, establishing a unidirectional sequence. This succession is defined as chronological, procedural, or logical. It is used to represent either a temporal order (e.g., in a workflow) or a logical order for processing and traversal (e.g., in an ordered list).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
